  <h2>Tips to save even more</h2>

  <p><strong>Ask about 90-day fills.</strong> Some insurance plans offer a lower per-month cost when you fill a 3-month supply at once. The Ozempic and Mounjaro savings cards also support 3-month fills.</p>

  <p><strong>Talk to your doctor about dose.</strong> Lower doses are cheaper across the board. If you're achieving good results at a moderate dose, there may be no clinical need to escalate — and the cost savings can be significant.</p>

  <p><strong>Consider the oral Wegovy pill.</strong> At $149/month for starting doses, it's now the cheapest branded GLP-1 option and eliminates the need for injections. The trade-off is that it must be taken daily on an empty stomach with a small amount of water.</p>

  <p><strong>Check GoodRx.</strong> Even with manufacturer pricing, it's worth checking GoodRx for pharmacy-specific pricing. Occasionally their coupons beat even the manufacturer self-pay price, and they can show you which nearby pharmacy has the lowest price.</p>

  <p><strong>Don't overlook Medicaid.</strong> If you're in one of the 13 states that covers GLP-1s for obesity through Medicaid, this could be your most affordable option. Check with your state's Medicaid programme for current coverage details.</p>

  <h2>The bottom line</h2>

  <p>The era of GLP-1 medications being out of reach for most people is ending. Between $25/month savings cards for insured patients, $50 Medicare copays, $149 oral Wegovy, and $199–350 TrumpRx pricing, there's now a realistic path to affordable treatment for nearly every situation.</p>

  <p>The most important step is having the conversation with your doctor. Many healthcare providers are still quoting the old $1,000+ list prices and may not be aware of how much the pricing landscape has changed. Come prepared with the specific options that apply to your situation, and you're far more likely to walk away with a prescription you can actually afford.</p>

  <p><em>Prices in this article are accurate as of February 2026. GLP-1 pricing is changing rapidly — check manufacturer websites and TrumpRx.gov for the most current offers. This article is for informational purposes only and does not constitute medical or financial advice.</em></p>

